{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-34506","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51185","text":"Portable Subject-Mode Closure — memo"}]},{"id":"blk-34507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51186","marks":["bold"],"text":"Slice:"},{"id":"spn-51187","text":" the correction ruled onto the top of the identity ladder, not a new rung. "},{"id":"spn-51188","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-51189","text":" shipped."}]},{"id":"blk-34508","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51190","marks":["bold"],"text":"Battery."},{"id":"spn-51191","text":" D31–D40 with the engine present: "},{"id":"spn-51192","marks":["bold"],"text":"10 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-51193","text":"; engine absent: "},{"id":"spn-51194","marks":["bold"],"text":"4 passed / 6 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-51195","text":" (D32, D37, D38 and D40 are recipient-side laws and need no Forge checkout — see §3). D1–D40: "},{"id":"spn-51196","marks":["bold"],"text":"40/40"},{"id":"spn-51197","text":" engine present, 16/24 engine absent. Whole tree: "},{"id":"spn-51198","marks":["bold"],"text":"474 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-51199","text":" across 26 files."}]},{"id":"blk-34509","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51200","text":"Ruled by the sixth GPT-5.6 ruling, which accepted "},{"id":"spn-51201","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-51202","text":" and then reproduced the caveat §6 of the previous memo had flagged:"}]},{"id":"blk-34510","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"source file mode:       0664\nmanifest mode:          0644\nbundle verification:    passes\ncanonical ZIP extract:  0644\nsame bundle_id:         yes          ← and yet\ndifferent snap-:        yes          ← so a different env-"},{"id":"blk-34511","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack directory        → bundle verifies, environment verifies\narchive-bundle        → normalizes 0664 → 0644\nextract archive       → bundle still verifies, environment FAILS to reopen"},{"id":"blk-34512","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51203","text":"It ruled that a reachable correctness defect, not an acceptable residual, and ordered it closed now."}]},{"id":"blk-34513","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51204","text":"1. Why the previous slice was wrong to ship it as a caveat"}]},{"id":"blk-34514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51205","text":"Both halves of the tension were individually correct and I could not see a way to weaken either, so I recorded the residual and moved on. That was the error. The residual is not a "},{"id":"spn-51206","marks":["italic"],"text":"tension between two identities"},{"id":"spn-51207","text":" — it is a "},{"id":"spn-51208","marks":["bold"],"text":"package that cannot survive its own archive"},{"id":"spn-51209","text":", and neither identity has to move to say so. The fix lives in a third place: "},{"id":"spn-51210","marks":["bold"],"text":"admission"},{"id":"spn-51211","text":". A mode that cannot be transported is refused before either id is minted."}]},{"id":"blk-34515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51212","text":"Stated the other way round: "},{"id":"spn-51213","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-51214","text":" sealing the exact mode is a claim about a repository, and "},{"id":"spn-51215","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-51216","text":" carrying the canonical mode is a claim about a distribution. There is no contradiction, only a set of repositories that are not distributable. TRAAVIIS packages distributions. So that set is inadmissible."}]},{"id":"blk-34516","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51217","text":"2. What was built"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34518","spans":[{"id":"spn-51218","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-34519","spans":[{"id":"spn-51219","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-34517","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34520","spans":[{"id":"spn-51220","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34521","spans":[{"id":"spn-51221","marks":["code"],"text":"CANONICAL_SUBJECT_MODES"},{"id":"spn-51222","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51223","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_subject_mode"},{"id":"spn-51224","text":", "},{"id":"spn-51225","marks":["code"],"text":"require_canonical_subject_modes"},{"id":"spn-51226","text":"; called from "},{"id":"spn-51227","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-51228","text":" Residency seams."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34522","spans":[{"id":"spn-51229","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34523","spans":[{"id":"spn-51230","marks":["code"],"text":"write_archive"},{"id":"spn-51231","text":" gated on a serialized round trip; new "},{"id":"spn-51232","marks":["code"],"text":"_verify_serialized"},{"id":"spn-51233","text":"; new refusal "},{"id":"spn-51234","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-51235","text":"; report gains "},{"id":"spn-51236","marks":["code"],"text":"roundtrip_verified"},{"id":"spn-51237","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34524","spans":[{"id":"spn-51238","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34525","spans":[{"id":"spn-51239","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE"},{"id":"spn-51240","text":"; every scaffolded file written at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-51241","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-51242","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34526","spans":[{"id":"spn-51243","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/cli.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34527","spans":[{"id":"spn-51244","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-51245","text":" relabels the legacy field "},{"id":"spn-51246","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"episode evidence\""},{"id":"spn-51247","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-51248","marks":["code"],"text":"archive-bundle"},{"id":"spn-51249","text":" prints the round-trip line."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34528","spans":[{"id":"spn-51250","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34529","spans":[{"id":"spn-51251","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-51252","text":" documented as a legacy episode-member field with a frozen value law."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34530","spans":[{"id":"spn-51253","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-34531","spans":[{"id":"spn-51254","text":"D31–D40."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34532","spans":[{"id":"spn-51255","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"}]},{"id":"blk-34533","spans":[{"id":"spn-51256","text":"new "},{"id":"spn-51257","marks":["bold"],"text":"§5c"},{"id":"spn-51258","text":" freezes both laws; §5b gains the "},{"id":"spn-51259","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-51260","text":" paragraph."}]}],[{"id":"blk-34534","spans":[{"id":"spn-51261","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"}]},{"id":"blk-34535","spans":[{"id":"spn-51262","text":"archive publication, a subject-mode section, and the legacy-field note."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34536","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51263","text":"The admission law"}]},{"id":"blk-34537","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51264","text":"For "},{"id":"spn-51265","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-51266","text":", every file whose mode enters "},{"id":"spn-51267","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-51268","text":" must already be exactly "},{"id":"spn-51269","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-51270","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-51271","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-51272","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-34538","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\"paths\": {\"src/tool.py\": {\"observed\": \"0664\", \"required\": \"0644\"}}}"},{"id":"blk-34539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51273","text":"typed "},{"id":"spn-51274","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SUBJECT_MODE_NONCANONICAL`"},{"id":"spn-51275","text":", raised from one shared helper called by "},{"id":"spn-51276","marks":["code"],"text":"recompute_subject_identity"},{"id":"spn-51277","text":" (authoring) and "},{"id":"spn-51278","marks":["code"],"text":"_reopen_subject"},{"id":"spn-51279","text":" (reopening, therefore also "},{"id":"spn-51280","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-51281","text":" and therefore "},{"id":"spn-51282","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-51283","text":"). That covers all three ways a nonportable package can appear: authored here, hand-built elsewhere, or authored before the law existed."}]},{"id":"blk-34540","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51284","text":"The helper reads "},{"id":"spn-51285","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-51286","text":" rather than walking the tree. That is the whole of D35: "},{"id":"spn-51287","marks":["code"],"text":"file_modes"},{"id":"spn-51288","text":" is already post-exclusion and already symlink-free, so an excluded file is out of scope "},{"id":"spn-51289","marks":["bold"],"text":"by construction"},{"id":"spn-51290","text":" rather than by a second glob match that could drift away from the first."}]},{"id":"blk-34541","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51291","marks":["code"],"text":"f\"{mode:04o}\""},{"id":"spn-51292","text":" renders set-ID modes as "},{"id":"spn-51293","marks":["code"],"text":"4755"},{"id":"spn-51294","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-51295","marks":["code"],"text":"2755"},{"id":"spn-51296","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-51297","marks":["code"],"text":"1644"},{"id":"spn-51298","text":", which are outside a two-element allowlist and are therefore refused without needing to be enumerated. The law is stated as an allowlist for exactly that reason."}]},{"id":"blk-34542","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51299","text":"The archive publication law"}]},{"id":"blk-34543","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"verify source tree\n→ write a temporary archive\n→ extract it to a temporary directory\n→ verify bundle closure from the extracted bytes\n→ when not --package-only, re-derive env- and subject closure too\n→ compare bundle_id and env_id\n→ atomically publish"},{"id":"blk-34544","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51300","text":"The old order verified the "},{"id":"spn-51301","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-51302","text":" and then serialized it, which proves the directory — not the artifact anyone receives. Anything serialization normalizes away was invisible to it, which is precisely how the mode defect could reach a published archive. A failed round trip raises "},{"id":"spn-51303","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-51304","text":" and leaves no archive at the output path."}]},{"id":"blk-34545","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51305","text":"3. D31–D40"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34547","spans":[{"id":"spn-51306","text":"#"}]},{"id":"blk-34548","spans":[{"id":"spn-51307","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-34549","spans":[{"id":"spn-51308","text":"test"}]}],"id":"blk-34546","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34550","spans":[{"id":"spn-51309","text":"D31"}]},{"id":"blk-34551","spans":[{"id":"spn-51310","text":"a Residency subject mode "},{"id":"spn-51311","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-51312","text":" is refused"}]},{"id":"blk-34552","spans":[{"id":"spn-51313","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d31_a_noncanonical_residency_subject_mode_is_refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34553","spans":[{"id":"spn-51314","text":"D32"}]},{"id":"blk-34554","spans":[{"id":"spn-51315","marks":["code"],"text":"0600"},{"id":"spn-51316","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-51317","marks":["code"],"text":"0640"},{"id":"spn-51318","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-51319","marks":["code"],"text":"0775"},{"id":"spn-51320","text":" / set-ID modes are refused too"}]},{"id":"blk-34555","spans":[{"id":"spn-51321","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d32_every_other_noncanonical_mode_is_refused_too"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34556","spans":[{"id":"spn-51322","text":"D33"}]},{"id":"blk-34557","spans":[{"id":"spn-51323","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-51324","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-51325","text":" subjects survive directory→ZIP→extract→verify"}]},{"id":"blk-34558","spans":[{"id":"spn-51326","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d33_canonical_0644_subjects_survive_directory_zip_extract_verify"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34559","spans":[{"id":"spn-51327","text":"D34"}]},{"id":"blk-34560","spans":[{"id":"spn-51328","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-51329","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-51330","text":" subjects survive the same path"}]},{"id":"blk-34561","spans":[{"id":"spn-51331","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d34_canonical_0755_subjects_survive_the_same_path"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34562","spans":[{"id":"spn-51332","text":"D35"}]},{"id":"blk-34563","spans":[{"id":"spn-51333","text":"excluded files' modes do not affect admission"}]},{"id":"blk-34564","spans":[{"id":"spn-51334","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d35_excluded_files_with_noncanonical_modes_do_not_affect_admission"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34565","spans":[{"id":"spn-51335","text":"D36"}]},{"id":"blk-34566","spans":[{"id":"spn-51336","text":"presentation modes may normalize without moving "},{"id":"spn-51337","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-34567","spans":[{"id":"spn-51338","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d36_presentation_modes_may_normalize_without_moving_the_environment"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34568","spans":[{"id":"spn-51339","text":"D37"}]},{"id":"blk-34569","spans":[{"id":"spn-51340","text":"publication verifies the extracted archive before rename"}]},{"id":"blk-34570","spans":[{"id":"spn-51341","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d37_archive_publication_verifies_the_extracted_archive_before_rename"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34571","spans":[{"id":"spn-51342","text":"D38"}]},{"id":"blk-34572","spans":[{"id":"spn-51343","text":"a failed round trip leaves no final archive"}]},{"id":"blk-34573","spans":[{"id":"spn-51344","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d38_a_failed_archive_roundtrip_leaves_no_final_archive"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34574","spans":[{"id":"spn-51345","text":"D39"}]},{"id":"blk-34575","spans":[{"id":"spn-51346","text":"ZIP and tar full "},{"id":"spn-51347","marks":["italic"],"text":"environment"},{"id":"spn-51348","text":" verification agree"}]},{"id":"blk-34576","spans":[{"id":"spn-51349","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d39_zip_and_tar_full_environment_verification_agree"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34577","spans":[{"id":"spn-51350","text":"D40"}]},{"id":"blk-34578","spans":[{"id":"spn-51351","text":"D1–D30 and the packet gates remain green"}]},{"id":"blk-34579","spans":[{"id":"spn-51352","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d40_the_earlier_laws_and_the_packet_gates_are_untouched"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51353","text":"D31 additionally proves both non-authoring seams: a hand-built package whose seal is "},{"id":"spn-51354","marks":["italic"],"text":"self-consistent"},{"id":"spn-51355","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-51356","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-51357","text":" is refused at reopen, and a scaffold written under "},{"id":"spn-51358","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-51359","text":" still packs (see §4)."}]},{"id":"blk-34581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51360","text":"D37 is observed at the publication seam — it spies "},{"id":"spn-51361","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-51362","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-51363","marks":["code"],"text":"os.replace"},{"id":"spn-51364","text":" and asserts that everything verified before publication was an "},{"id":"spn-51365","marks":["bold"],"text":"extraction"},{"id":"spn-51366","text":", never the source directory. D38 drives both failure modes: a closure failure out of the extraction, and a round trip that verifies cleanly as some "},{"id":"spn-51367","marks":["italic"],"text":"other"},{"id":"spn-51368","text":" package, which is the branch that catches silent normalization."}]},{"id":"blk-34582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51369","text":"D40 is a completeness check, not a re-run: D1–D30 are re-run by the battery itself, in the same process, every time. What D40 asserts is that no earlier law was dropped or renamed (the D-numbers are exactly 1..40), that the source-release gate learned nothing about either new code, and that "},{"id":"spn-51370","marks":["code"],"text":"TrvmWorldV1"},{"id":"spn-51371","text":" did "},{"id":"spn-51372","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-51373","text":" inherit the mode law while "},{"id":"spn-51374","marks":["code"],"text":"ResidencyRepositoryV1"},{"id":"spn-51375","text":" enforces it at exactly two seams."}]},{"id":"blk-34583","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51376","text":"4. A defect this slice created and then closed"}]},{"id":"blk-34584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51377","text":"Adding the admission law immediately broke "},{"id":"spn-51378","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-51379","text":" on any machine with a loose umask. "},{"id":"spn-51380","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.materialize"},{"id":"spn-51381","text":" wrote every file at the process umask default, so under "},{"id":"spn-51382","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-51383","text":" a freshly scaffolded environment is "},{"id":"spn-51384","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-51385","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-51386","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-51387","text":" now — correctly — refuses it. Every author on a "},{"id":"spn-51388","marks":["code"],"text":"002"},{"id":"spn-51389","text":" machine would have been locked out by their first two commands."}]},{"id":"blk-34585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51390","text":"It was invisible here only because this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-51391","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 022"},{"id":"spn-51392","text":", so the default coincided with the declared mode. Exactly the same shape as the latent defect the previous slice closed, from exactly the same cause: a template's modes are part of the template, and were being taken from the machine that unpacked it."}]},{"id":"blk-34586","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51393","text":"Closed by writing every scaffolded file at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-51394","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE = 0o644"},{"id":"spn-51395","text":" (and the scaffold root at "},{"id":"spn-51396","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-51397","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-51398","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-51399","text":" under a restrictive umask does not emit a "},{"id":"spn-51400","marks":["code"],"text":"0700"},{"id":"spn-51401","text":" environment either). D31 pins it with a real "},{"id":"spn-51402","marks":["code"],"text":"os.umask(0o002)"},{"id":"spn-51403","text":" scaffold that must still pack to the reference "},{"id":"spn-51404","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-51405","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34587","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-51406","text":"5. "},{"id":"spn-51407","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-51408","text":" — kept, relabelled"}]},{"id":"blk-34588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51409","text":"Ruled: do "},{"id":"spn-51410","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-51411","text":" rename it. Done, and the strengthened D27 reading was confirmed correct. What changed is only ambiguity:"}]},{"id":"blk-34589","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51412","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-51413","text":" prints "},{"id":"spn-51414","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode evidence: …`"},{"id":"spn-51415","text":", on both the human and the"}]}],"id":"blk-34590","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51416","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-51417","text":" stderr line. It no longer prints the word \"bundle\" for this field."}]},{"id":"blk-34593","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-51418","marks":["code"],"text":"evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-51419","text":" documents it as a "},{"id":"spn-51420","marks":["bold"],"text":"legacy episode-member field"},{"id":"spn-51421","text":" with a froz